    "title": "Researchers uncover solar wind event that may explain Uranus' strange magnetic behavior - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Sindhura Venkatesh ,\n1 hours ago Space.com reports that new analysis of Voyager 2 data suggests Uranus may have been experiencing a strong solar wind event during the spacecraft’s 1986 flyby. Researchers revisited the measurements almost 40 years later and found signs that a fast stream of solar wind may have collided with a slower one, forming what is known as a co-rotating interaction region. Read full article\nRead in NewsBreak",
